        "id": "acffa2-ch6-q01",
        "qText": "The financial year end of Global Co is 30 June 20X3. An inventory count conducted on 7 July 20X3 showed inventory valued at $950,000. Between 30 June and 7 July, purchases were $60,000, goods returned to suppliers were $4,000, and sales were $100,000 (at a constant gross profit margin of 30%). What is the correct inventory value at 30 June 20X3?",
        "type": "single",
        "options": [
          "$964,000",
          "$936,000",
          "$974,000",
          "$926,000"
        ],
        "correct": 0,
        "working": "Cost of goods sold between 30 June and 7 July = $100,000 x (1 - 0.30) = $70,000. To roll back inventory from 7 July to 30 June: Inventory at 30 June = Inventory at 7 July ($950,000) + Cost of sales ($70,000) - Purchases ($60,000) + Purchase returns ($4,000) = $964,000.",
        "romanUrdu": "30 June ki inventory = 7 July count ($950,000) + Sale ki cost ($70,000) - Khareedari ($60,000) + Wapas kiya gaya maal ($4,000) = $964,000.",
