        "correct": 3,
        "working": "According to ACCA MA1 Exam Kit (Question 3.26), the correct option is D ('Production costs:'). ACCA examining team comments Contribution is the difference between sales revenue and variable costs (both production and non- production). It is the contribution towards covering fixed costs and providing some profit. Contribution per unit is $5.30 [sales revenue $11.20 – (variable production costs $5.40 + variable non-production overhead $0.50)]. This then needs to be multiplied by the units sold to calculate the total contribution for the period which is $44,520 (8,400 units sold @ $5.30 per unit ",
        "romanUrdu": "ACCA MA1 Exam Kit ke mutabiq sahi jawab Option D ('Production costs:') hai.",
        "examTip": "CBE exam mein questions aur data tables ko ehtiyat se parhein."
